# Caravan Navigation — Privacy Policy

This policy covers the Caravan Navigation app and takes precedence over the
[general policy](README.md). The Developer operates no servers and receives no data from
the app.

## What is sent, and to whom

Routes and address searches are provided by **Geoapify** (Geoapify GmbH). To do this the
app sends Geoapify, over an encrypted HTTPS connection:

- the start, destination and any waypoints of a route, which may be your current
  location;
- the text of an address or place you search for;
- the routing mode for your vehicle class (for example "light truck");
- the Geoapify API key configured in the app.

These are sent only when you plan a route, recalculate one, or search for a place. Your
position is **not** sent continuously while you drive. Turn-by-turn guidance is worked
out on your device.

Geoapify's handling of this data is described in its privacy policy:
https://www.geoapify.com/privacy-policy/

The map itself is drawn by Apple Maps (iOS) or Google Maps (Android), which receive the
map area being displayed, under their own privacy policies.

## Location

The app asks for your location to plan routes from where you are and to guide you. While
you are navigating it keeps using your location in the background (for example with the
screen locked) so spoken directions continue; this stops when navigation ends. You can
withdraw permission at any time in your device's settings, and you can still plan routes
between typed addresses without it.

## What stays on your device

Your settings, vehicle profile (dimensions and weight) and saved or recent places are
stored only on your device, in the app's own storage. They are not sent anywhere and are
removed when you delete the app.

## What is not collected

No account, name, email address, contacts or advertising identifier is collected. No
analytics, advertising, tracking or crash-reporting services are used, and nothing is
sold or shared for advertising.

## Children

The app is not directed at children under 13.

